<BaseLayout title="Fluids and capacities">
  <h1>Fluids and capacities</h1>
  <p>Use the fluid specification for the exact engine, transmission, and market. The figures below are from Volvo's 2021 S60 owner-information tables where the listed engine code matches. Confirm the vehicle's engine and gearbox codes before purchasing or filling fluids.</p>

  <h2>Engine oil — identify the engine first</h2>
  <p>Volvo's 2021 S60 support tables list the following four-cylinder gasoline engine alternatives with the same approximate oil volume and grade. The table spans market-specific engine alternatives; not every listed code was offered in North America:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Engine designation</th><th>Engine code listed by Volvo</th><th>Oil grade</th><th>Approx. volume incl. filter</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th>T5</th><td>B4204T26</td><td>Castrol Edge Professional V 0W-20 or VCC RBS0-2AE 0W-20</td><td>5.6 L</td></tr>
      <tr><th>T5 / T5 AWD</th><td>B4204T23</td><td>Castrol Edge Professional V 0W-20 or VCC RBS0-2AE 0W-20</td><td>5.6 L</td></tr>
      <tr><th>T5 AWD</th><td>B4204T20</td><td>Castrol Edge Professional V 0W-20 or VCC RBS0-2AE 0W-20</td><td>5.6 L</td></tr>
      <tr><th>T6 AWD</th><td>B4204T27</td><td>Castrol Edge Professional V 0W-20 or VCC RBS0-2AE 0W-20</td><td>5.6 L</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note"><strong>T8 Recharge:</strong> do not assume the gasoline-only table above applies to every T8 engine code or market. Confirm the exact T8 engine code and oil specification in the vehicle-specific Volvo manual or service system. Hybrid-system coolant circuits are separate from the ordinary engine-oil service.</p>
  <p>The volume is approximate: do not pour the full nominal capacity in blindly. Follow the correct service procedure and verify the electronic oil-level reading under the conditions specified in the owner's manual. Volvo says not to use oil additives.</p>

  <h2>Coolant</h2>
  <p>Use Volvo-approved coolant for the installed powertrain and follow the correct premix/concentrate instructions for the market. Do not mix incompatible coolant types. Never open a hot or pressurized cooling system. T8 Recharge has additional hybrid-system thermal circuits; do not treat every coolant reservoir or circuit as interchangeable.</p>

  <h2>Brake fluid</h2>
  <p>Volvo specifies original fluid or an equivalent meeting the combined DOT 4, DOT 5.1, and ISO 4925 Class 6 requirements in the cited owner information. Confirm the exact specification for the vehicle and have hydraulic-system service performed using the correct Volvo procedure. Brake fluid is hygroscopic and should not be selected by color or brand alone.</p>

  <h2>Automatic transmission fluid</h2>
  <p>Volvo lists different fluids by gearbox: TG-81SC uses AW-1, while AWF8G45/AWF8G55 use AW-2 in the referenced documentation. T5, T6, and T8 applications may not use the same gearbox variant. Identify the gearbox by VIN or transmission designation before purchasing fluid; never choose AW-1 or AW-2 from the engine badge or AWD label alone. Fluid level and temperature procedures are transmission-specific.</p>

  <h2>Washer fluid</h2>
  <p>Use automotive windshield-washer fluid suitable for the expected outside temperature. In freezing weather, use a winter-rated product and avoid plain water. The headlamp-washer system, where fitted, uses the same washer-fluid supply.</p>

  <h2>Do not guess these values</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Coolant system total capacity and drain/refill quantity.</li>
    <li>Transmission service-fill quantity and temperature/check procedure.</li>
    <li>Brake hydraulic system total capacity and bleeding sequence.</li>
    <li>Refrigerant type and charge quantity.</li>
    <li>T8 high-voltage battery and hybrid thermal-system service fluids.</li>
  </ul>

